{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2354 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "e59af7d7bc14721c5afd0fbbe8ff70066dd063e1fc3cd71250e97e28fab3965a" :edb/db-before-t 2353 :edb/db-after-t 2354 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535666 50 #inst "2026-10-09T04:43:23.112Z" 13194139535666 true] [17592186124423 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360056 13194139535666 true] [17592186124423 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360070 13194139535666 true] [17592186124477 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360063 13194139535666 true] [17592186124839 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535666 true] [17592186124839 1100 "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the hyperbolic paraboloid $z - 3 = ((x - 5)^{2})/(5) - \\frac{y^{2}}{4}$?" 13194139535666 false] [17592186124839 1100 "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the hyperbolic paraboloid $z-3=\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}?$" 13194139535666 true] [17592186124839 1145 "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the paraboloid, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-3 & =\\frac{(0-5)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ z-3 & =\\frac{25}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ z-3 & =5-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ z-8 & =-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-4(z-8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives us the equation of the parabola in $yz$-plane." 13194139535666 true] [17592186124847 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535666 true] [17592186124847 1100 "Given the elliptic paraboloid $z + 4 = \\frac{x^{2}}{4} + ((y - 4)^{2})/(4)$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." 13194139535666 false] [17592186124847 1100 "Given the elliptic paraboloid $z+4=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{4}$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." 13194139535666 true] [17592186124847 1145 "To find the $x$-intercepts of the paraboloid, we substitute $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation of the paraboloid and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+4 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0-4)^{2}}{4} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{16}{4} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+4 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the solution $x=0$\n\nTherefore, the intercept with the $x$-axis is $(0,0,0)$ only." 13194139535666 true] [17592186360056 1017 #edb/ref 17592186360057 13194139535666 true] [17592186360056 1089 "q-164273" 13194139535666 true] [17592186360056 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535666 true] [17592186360056 1100 "Find the saddle point of the hyperbolic paraboloid $z+4=\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{3}.$" 13194139535666 true] [17592186360056 1113 #uuid "c12711ba-8eec-56d7-b5e7-2963addec53e" 13194139535666 true] [17592186360056 1145 "The general equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid with a saddle point at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is \n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo find the saddle point, we rewrite our equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+4 & =\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ z-(-4) & =\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid with a saddle point at $(3,-1,-4).$" 13194139535666 true] [17592186360057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360058 13194139535666 true] [17592186360057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360059 13194139535666 true] [17592186360057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360060 13194139535666 true] [17592186360057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360061 13194139535666 true] [17592186360057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360062 13194139535666 true] [17592186360057 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535666 true] [17592186360057 1041 "selection" 13194139535666 true] [17592186360057 1104 #edb/ref 17592186360062 13194139535666 true] [17592186360057 1110 #uuid "882fdc94-66dd-5350-a4b1-9d09e841c0a0" 13194139535666 true] [17592186360058 1034 "(3,4,-1)" 13194139535666 true] [17592186360058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535666 true] [17592186360058 1111 #uuid "3987f7d3-8518-5cd6-828a-8d0b7c9995f6" 13194139535666 true] [17592186360059 1034 "(1,-3,-4)" 13194139535666 true] [17592186360059 1103 #edb/ref 175921860